#ASSERT `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a limb answered JUST FALSE is not a made-out limb
#ASSERT `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 121(1)(a) made out
#ASSERT `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 121(1)(b) made out
#ASSERT `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 121(1)(c) made out
#ASSERT `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 121(1)(d) made out
#ASSERT `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 121(1)(e) made out
